  "notes": "ABC-Bench (Agentic Backend Coding Benchmark) evaluates agents across the complete backend development lifecycle. Unlike benchmarks that focus on isolated code editing, ABC-Bench requires end-to-end tasks from repository exploration to containerized service deployment.\n\n224 tasks from 127 MIT-licensed open-source repos:\n- 8 programming languages: Python, JavaScript, Java, Go, Ruby, C#, PHP, Rust\n- 19 major backend frameworks: Spring Boot, Express, Rails, Laravel, FastAPI, Gin, ASP.NET Core, etc.\n- 132 logic implementation tasks + 92 full-lifecycle tasks\n\nKey findings:\n- Environment configuration is the primary bottleneck, not code logic\n- Rust is a critical performance bottleneck (most models score 0%)\n- Interaction depth strongly correlates with success (Pearson r = 0.87)\n\nFrom Dawning Road and OpenMOSS."
